  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 345 AM CDT Sun Oct 4 3456\n\nMonday night, surface winds finally veer back to return flow, \nallowing more respectable temperatures to come into the picture.  A \ngradual warming trend is forecast through at least midweek, when \nhighs top out ~ 5-7 F above normal.  At about this time, long-range \nmodels begin developing an upper trough directly over West Texas and \nSoutheast New Mexico, decreasing thicknesses and lowering highs by \nup to 3-4 F Thursday through Saturday.  Wednesday through Friday, \nmodels develop convection over Chihuahua, bringing it across the \nriver and farther north each day.  Something to watch will be deep \neasterly flow saturating GFS soundings at KMAF to 300 mb by 18Z \nFriday, yielding PWATs of almost 1.5\", or around the 99th percentile \naccording to climatology.  A boundary Friday afternoon to tap into \nthis would make for a nice weekend, and bears watching.  Stay tuned.",
